# Force LF in the working tree for every text file, regardless of the
# cloning machine's core.autocrlf. Without this, a Windows/WSL client with
# autocrlf=true checks the .chezmoiscripts/*.sh.tmpl out with CRLF; chezmoi
# renders that straight into the executed script, the shebang becomes
# "#!/bin/sh\r", and the kernel can't find that interpreter — chezmoi reports
# it as "fork/exec <script>: no such file or directory", which is really a
# missing-interpreter error one level down.
* text=auto eol=lf
